WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.070
Many people think the idea of a soul
being reborn belongs only to Hinduism and

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.230
Buddhism.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.840
Yet some Jews today believe a
soul can return to this world,

4
00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.460
to finish work it left undone.

5
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.140
Other Jews reject the idea completely.

6
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:19.800
So where does the idea of a soul
returning to finish its work come from?

7
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.260
In this mission, you'll explore Kabbalah,

8
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.620
and ask who really wrote
its most famous book.

9
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.810
Then you'll find out which
Jews accept a returning soul,

10
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.980
and why others reject it.

11
00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:35.370
Your mission: trace where the idea
of a returning soul comes from,

12
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.410
and who in Judaism holds it.
